import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>4.6 (Day 1) — Dungeon Crawler RPG Build: Combat &amp; Duel Engine</h1>

<p>
    <strong>CED Topics 2.1, 2.9 · 90-Minute RPG Build (Day 1 of 2).</strong> Over the next two
    classes you will build <code>DungeonLoop.java</code> — combining indeterminate
    <code>while</code> loops (for combat rounds until one fighter falls) with fixed-count
    <code>for</code> loops (for rooms and multi-floor campaigns). Today you complete Parts 1 and 2;
    next class (<code>4.6b</code>) you build floor exploration and the multi-floor campaign.
</p>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Starting Files (Download All Three into the Same Folder):</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <a href="../data/DungeonLoop.java" download>DungeonLoop.java</a> — bare-minimum
            compiling stub for both days of the 4.6 build.
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="../data/DungeonLoopCheck.java" download>DungeonLoopCheck.java</a> — automated
            acceptance test suite (13 checks across Parts 1–4).
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="../data/Dice.java" download>Dice.java</a> — your dice engine from Unit 1.7.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <pre><code>javac Dice.java DungeonLoop.java DungeonLoopCheck.java
java DungeonLoopCheck</code></pre>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Part 1 · Discovery &amp; Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~45 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 1: <code>simulateDuelToDeath(int playerHP, int playerDmgPerHit, int monsterHP, int monsterDmgPerHit)</code></h3>

    <p>
        Before adding dice randomness, build the deterministic duel engine that <code>DungeonLoopCheck</code>
        and tomorrow's floor crawler both rely on:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Loop <strong>while both combatants are alive</strong>
            (<code>playerHP &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; monsterHP &gt; 0</code>).</li>
        <li>In each round:
            <ol>
                <li>The player strikes first: subtract <code>playerDmgPerHit</code> from
                    <code>monsterHP</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Only if <code>monsterHP &gt; 0</code></strong>, the monster strikes back:
                    subtract <code>monsterDmgPerHit</code> from <code>playerHP</code>.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li>When the loop ends, return the player's remaining HP — <strong>clamped at
            <code>0</code></strong> if <code>playerHP</code> dropped below <code>0</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Discovery Trap: Using <code>||</code> Instead of <code>&amp;&amp;</code> in a Duel Loop</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>What happens if a student writes
                <code>while (playerHP &gt; 0 || monsterHP &gt; 0)</code> ("keep fighting while
                someone is alive") instead of <code>&amp;&amp;</code>? Trace what happens after the
                monster dies on Round 2 while the player still has <code>15 HP</code>!</li>
            <li>Apply De Morgan's Law: the duel stops when
                <code>playerHP &lt;= 0 || monsterHP &lt;= 0</code>. Negate that stop condition to
                prove why the continuation condition must use <code>&amp;&amp;</code>.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Part 2 · Live Dice Combat</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~45 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 2: <code>runCombat(...)</code></h3>

    <p>
        Now implement the live dice-driven combat loop using <code>Dice.roll(...)</code>:
    </p>
    <pre><code>public static boolean runCombat(String playerName, int playerHP, int playerAC,
                                int playerAttackBonus, String monsterName,
                                int monsterHP, int monsterAC,
                                int monsterAttackBonus, int monsterDamageDie)</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>Loop while <code>playerHP &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; monsterHP &gt; 0</code>:
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Player attack:</strong> Roll <code>int d20 = Dice.roll(20);</code>. A
                    natural <code>20</code> deals <code>Dice.roll(8) * 2</code> damage; a natural
                    <code>1</code> deals <code>0</code>; otherwise if
                    <code>d20 + playerAttackBonus &gt;= monsterAC</code>, deal
                    <code>Dice.roll(8)</code> damage. Subtract from <code>monsterHP</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Monster counterattack (only if <code>monsterHP &gt; 0</code>):</strong>
                    Roll <code>int m20 = Dice.roll(20);</code>. If
                    <code>m20 + monsterAttackBonus &gt;= playerAC</code>, subtract
                    <code>Dice.roll(monsterDamageDie)</code> from <code>playerHP</code>.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li>Return <code>true</code> if <code>playerHP &gt; 0</code> (player won), or
            <code>false</code> otherwise.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Day 1 Milestone — Done When</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>All <strong>6 checks in Parts 1 and 2</strong> of <code>java DungeonLoopCheck</code> report <code>PASS</code></li>
            <li>You have completed the reflection boxes above and downloaded your <code>.json</code> for Canvas</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/dungeon-system.html">Dungeon Loop System (Student RPG Guide)</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/while-loops.html">while Loops</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
